    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1c294f8d_02d0202f",
        "filename": "cc/cc.go",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 1838,
      "author": {
        "id": 1066075
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-19T07:30:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Factor this code out so that it\u0027s not duplicated between `GenerateAndroidBuildActions()` and `HandleBazelMetadata()`\n\nIt\u0027s long and mysterious enough (at least to me) that there is a large risk of the two copies coming out of sync.\n\nMaybe you can move `maybeInstall()` above the `HandleBazelMetadata()` call and remove that little duplication also?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1824,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1838,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "88b36f693674e1bfd9ea4721d8b5ae53c83f9f37",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "93c97e65_c3118fff",
        "filename": "cc/cc.go",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 1838,
      "author": {
        "id": 1605027
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-19T22:47:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "maybeInstall has to come after HandleBazelMetadata, because the installer implementation may require properties set by HandleBazelMetadata.\n\nIf we reorder these two lines, we get:\n\n```\nerror: external/libcap/Android.bp:133:1: module \"cap_names.h\": host tool \"_makenames\" missing output file\n17:11:38 soong bootstrap failed with: exit status 1\n```\n\nI also wanted to originally refactor common pieces between bazel mode and soong mode, but I don\u0027t think this is an improvement:\n\nWe want to keep the non-bazelHandler piece of this function small. Having the two copies coming out of sync is mostly ok, because we don\u0027t want functionally added to the bazel function without thinking more about it.\n\nAlso, I don\u0027t think there\u0027s much semantic meaning to the common piece.\n\nThat said, tinkering with this again has allowed me to reduce the function a bit.\n\nWhat do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "1c294f8d_02d0202f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1824,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1838,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "88b36f693674e1bfd9ea4721d8b5ae53c83f9f37",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cd3cdc55_e8bb84b6",
        "filename": "cc/cc.go",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 1880,
      "author": {
        "id": 1066075
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-19T07:30:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it by design that this code is not evaluated in mixed mode?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1878,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 1880,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "88b36f693674e1bfd9ea4721d8b5ae53c83f9f37",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
